d/t_thumb/sc16kor.jpg"}, {"id": 1986364, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16kos.jpg"}, {"id": 1986365, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16kot.jpg"}, {"id": 1986366, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16kou.jpg"}, {"id": 1986367, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16kov.jpg"}], "slug": "siege-and-settle", "summary": "Siege & Settle is a free-to-play real-time strategy MMO played in the web browser.\nPlayers start with one village, develop its resource fields and buildings, train troops and found or conquer new villages.\n\nThree tribes are available (Romans, Germanic Tribes and Dacians), each with ten units. Barbarian villages raid every player and guard artifacts.\nEach world ends: alliances compete to hold eleven control points (ruins, towers and shrines) until one side reaches the world's target score. Classic worlds are for human players only; in Bot worlds players can also connect their own programs or AI agents through a REST API or an MCP server, under the same rules. Each world has a public chronicle and the rules are documented in a public wiki.", "themes": [{"id": 22, "name": "Historical"}, {"id": 39, "name": "Warfare"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/siege-and-settle", "game_localizations": [{"id": 64006, "region": {"id": 4, "name": "Europe", "category": "continent", "identifier": "EU"}}]}